@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning XSS
	Testing to assure that the provisioning site has no XSS vulnerabilities.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| svg.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I log out and log into the koroneiki homepage as "koroneiki.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the koroneiki account index page
	* I tear down the following accounts via the koroneiki frontend
	| ><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>  |
	| ><svg /onload=alert(/parent/)> |

Scenario: View XSS
	Testing XSS vulnerabilities on the provisioning page

	Given I log into the koroneiki homepage as "koroneiki.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the koroneiki contact index page
	And I click on the new entity button
	And I populate and save the entity form with the following values
	| First Name    | Input | '"><svg /onload=alert(/contact/)>    |
	| Middle Name   | Input | '"><svg /onload=alert(/contact/)>    |
	| Last Name     | Input | '"><svg /onload=alert(/contact/)>    |
	| Email Address | Input | svg.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I click on the new account button
	And I populate and save the account form with the following values
	| Name           | Input  | '"><svg /onload=alert(/parent/)> |
	| Code           | Input  | '"><svg /onload=alert(/parent/)> |
	| Tier           | Select | Regular                          |
	| Support Region | Select | United States                    |
	| Status         | Select | Approved                         |
	And I click on the new account button
	And I populate and save the account form with the following values
	| Name           | Input  | '"><svg /onload=alert(/child/)> |
	| Code           | Input  | '"><svg /onload=alert(/child/)> |
	| Tier           | Select | Regular                         |
	| Support Region | Select | United States                   |
	| Status         | Select | Approved                        |
	When I search the accounts page using the keyword "><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>"
	And I click on the account with the name "><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I click on the assign contact button
	And I populate and save the assign contact form with the following values
	| Email Address | svg.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Assign Role   | Member                               |
	And I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	And I click on the assign worker button
	And I populate and save the assign worker form with the following values
	| Email Address | svg.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Assign Role   | Member                               |
	And I click on the "Details" tab
	And I edit the following account fields and types to the following values under the account details tab
	| Parent | Select Entity | ><svg /onload=alert(/parent/)> | |
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>"
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the account with the name "><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>" on the provisioning index
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Details" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Teams" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Related Accounts" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Approved" related account tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then I should not see an alert
	When I click on the "Teams" tab
	And I click on the "><svg /onload=alert(/child/)>" team link
	Then I should not see an alert
